    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two are support classes), and it passes. The full `mvn test` build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required de-duplicating a colliding `customerCode` by appending `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\nI modified `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`):\n\n- It still computes the deterministic base code `<REGION>-<HASH8>` as before.\n- It now also injects the `OwnerRepository`, collects all existing owners' `customerCode` values into a set, and if the base code is already taken, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 choosing the smallest `n \u2265 2` that yields a code not in use. The final unique code is set on the owner.\n\nThis step runs before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner isn't yet persisted and doesn't count itself as a collision. This follows the existing repository-scanning pattern used by sibling functions like `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` and `CountOwnerNamesakes`.\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` passes and `mvn test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 test, 0 failures).",
